    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1316">

                <pb facs="1130" n="1026" xml:id="pg1026"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 711.13/34.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                            American Minister to Coata Rica.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1913-09-20">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">September 20, 1913</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>In regard to Salvador’s invitation reported in your September 19, you may if
                    opportune suggest to Costa Rica that its acceptance should be based upon the
                    willingness of Nicaragua to attend such a conference rather than merely on the
                    extending of an invitation to Nicaragua.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
